  "summary": "004F8710 and 004D8C00 are __cdecl varargs setters terminated by a zero id. Each replaces level 4 of a five-level (screens) or four-level (input contexts) stack of std::vector<int> and then re-derives the whole state: 004F7620 recomputes the +4h requested byte of all 95 registered screens with an occlusion floor at 00E08310, and 004C4300 pushes input-context priorities into the input manager. An empty list clears its level, which is how the front end hides everything. 00687330 is the multi menu's interface-id-to-screen-id table.",
  "calling_conventions": {
    "004f8710": {
      "convention": "__cdecl varargs",
      "args": "id..., 0",
      "ret": "RET",
      "seh_handler": "00c68558",
      "level": 4,
      "vector": "00e18d28"
    },
    "004d8c00": {
      "convention": "__cdecl varargs",
      "args": "game, id..., 0",
      "ret": "RET",
      "seh_handler": "00c66568",
      "level": 4,
      "vector": "game+5a0h"
    },
    "004f7620": {
      "convention": "__cdecl",
      "args": "none",
      "ret": "RET"
    },
    "004f83b0": {
      "convention": "__thiscall(screen)",
      "args": "none",
      "ret": "RET",
      "seh_handler": "00c684d8"
    },
    "00687330": {
      "convention": "id at [ESP+4], ECX loaded but unused at the caller",
      "args": "int interfaceId",
      "ret": "RET 4",
      "note": "__thiscall ignoring this is as consistent as the __stdcall in docs/FRONTEND_MANAGERS.md; the callee cannot distinguish them"
    },
    "004c4300": {
      "convention": "__thiscall(game, int level)",
      "args": "int level",
      "ret": "RET 4"
    },
    "004f7210": {
      "convention": "__thiscall(vector)",
      "args": "none",
      "ret": "RET",
      "role": "std::vector<int>::size"
    },
    "004f81d0": {
      "convention": "__thiscall(dst, src)",
      "args": "src",
      "ret": "RET 4",
      "role": "std::vector<int>::operator="
    },
    "004f8480": {
      "convention": "__thiscall(vector, const int*)",
      "args": "const int*",
      "ret": "RET 4",
      "role": "std::vector<int>::push_back"
