  "commit_004f83b0": {
    "convention": "__thiscall(screen), RET, SEH 00c684d8",
    "behaviour": "the screen's virtual +24h fills a heap vector of child pointers; every non-null child gets its own virtual +34h called with the byte at screen+5h, the applied state, not the requested one; then the vector is freed",
    "base_collect": "004f75d0, ret 4, so a screen with no children commits nothing",
    "callers": 35,
    "prior_ledger_name": "BSP_FrontEndScreen_n in config/names/004f0000.jsonl, superseded here"
  },
  "corrections": [
    "include/bsp/frontend_managers.hpp calls both varargs lists interface sets. They carry two different id spaces: 004f8710 takes screen registry slots, 004d8c00 takes input-context ids 1..19h.",
    "docs/FRONTEND_MANAGERS.md records 00687330 as __stdcall(int id). The caller at 00687838 also loads ECX, so a __thiscall that ignores this fits the same bytes."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "No leaf override of the screen base virtual +4h or +8h was identified, so the occlusion and exemption rules have no observed instance.",
    "Levels 1, 2, 3 and 5 have no recovered publisher other than the 004da780 teardown.",
    "Nothing was found that reads 00e18cdc between the setter that raises it and the pump that clears it, so 'dirty' is a hypothesis.",
    "The dead backwards scan at 004d8c84 is unexplained.",
    "The 16-byte vector's +0h word is never initialised by these callers; the _SECURE_SCL container-proxy reading is inferred from the 00bf6713 assertions, not traced to a writer.",
    "005b5757 reads 00e08310 and was not examined."
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "Find the screens that override +8h (occluding) and +4h (self-managed).",
    "Identify the screen types behind registry slots 0Ch and 15h.",
    "Trace the callers of 004f8530, 004f85d0, 004f8670 and 004f87b0 to name levels 1, 2, 3, 5.",
    "Name the input contexts 1..19h that 004c4300 prioritises."
  ],
